  "content": {
    "id": "p11-q9-response",
    "type": "question",
    "label": "9",
    "prompt": "By expanding the right-hand side, show that\n$$a^n-b^n=(a-b)(a^{n-1}+a^{n-2}b+\\cdots+ab^{n-2}+b^{n-1}).$$",
    "layout": "list",
    "columns": null,
    "questionDiagrams": [],
    "children": [],
    "answer": {
      "short": "$a^n-b^n$.\n\nExpanding cancels every intermediate term.",
      "worked": "The terms obtained by multiplying by $a$ cancel the corresponding terms obtained by multiplying by $-b$:\n$$\\begin{align*}(a-b)(a^{n-1}+a^{n-2}b+\\cdots+b^{n-1})&=\\sum_{j=0}^{n-1}a^{n-j}b^j-\\sum_{j=0}^{n-1}a^{n-1-j}b^{j+1}\\\\(a-b)(a^{n-1}+a^{n-2}b+\\cdots+b^{n-1})&=a^n+\\sum_{j=1}^{n-1}a^{n-j}b^j-\\sum_{j=1}^{n-1}a^{n-j}b^j-b^n\\\\(a-b)(a^{n-1}+a^{n-2}b+\\cdots+b^{n-1})&=a^n-b^n.\\end{align*}$$",
      "solutionDiagrams": []
    },
    "answerSpaceMm": 48
  },
